  "body": "Direct-PR: tracker bookkeeping after #167.\n\n- The five pending captures #167 kept in LOTS.md ('Not an issue yet') are now issues #264–#268 (two MVP-priority public-write captures for LOT-048, three for LOT-034/035); the table is removed and the capture line lists them.\n- `.github/rulesets/dev-swift.json`: `strict_required_status_checks_policy` false, matching the owner's change of 2026-10-28 (the file is settings as code; the live ruleset already has it).\n\ncheck-lot-deps and markdownlint pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHteTFWfkJGeSNGpSW\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated the capture backlog documentation to list pending captures associated with issues 264–268 and clarify that each new pending capture requires its own issue.\n  * The table of uncaptured states and its accompanying note are no longer included. No user-facing product behavior changes are noted.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
